  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Which of the following is a factor of $-{v}^{2}+12v-45?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we let $f(v)=-{v}^{2}+12v-45.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(v)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(v) & =0 \\\\ -{v}^{2}+12v-45 & =0 \\\\ {v}^{2}-12v+45 & =0 \\\\ ({v}^{2}-2\\cdot 6\\cdot v+{6}^{2})-{6}^{2}+45 & =0 \\\\ (v-6)^{2}-36+45 & =0 \\\\ (v-6)^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ (v-6)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ (v-6)^{2} & =9{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (v-6)^{2} & =(3\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ v-6 & =\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ v & =6\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our quadratic equation has roots ${v}_{1}=6+3\\text{i}$ and ${v}_{2}=6-3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-1,$ the expression $-{v}^{2}+12v-45$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{v}^{2}+12v-45 & =a(v-{v}_{1})(v-{v}_{2}) \\\\  & =-(v-(6+3\\text{i}))(v-(6-3\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, among the given options, only $v-(6-3\\text{i})$ is a factor of $-{v}^{2}+12v-45.$",
